---
// Three slices built from a := make([]int, 3, 4) share one backing array of four slots.
// Numbers match the captured go run output in the post: [0 0 0] [0 0 0 2] [0 0 0 2], len 3 cap 4.
const W = 900;
const H = 300;
const X0 = 300;
const CELL = 100;
const cells = [0, 0, 0, 2];
---
<figure class="gp20a">
  <div class="gp20a-scroll">
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="One backing array with four slots holding 0, 0, 0 and 2. Slice a covers the first three slots. Slices b and c both cover all four slots, so the 2 written by the second append replaced the 1 written by the first.">
    <text x="20" y="26" class="h">
      <tspan data-lang-en>One backing array, three slices</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Một mảng nền, ba slice</tspan>
    </text>

    {cells.map((v, i) => (
      <>
        <rect x={X0 + i * CELL} y="50" width={CELL} height="50" class={i === 3 ? 'hot' : 'box'} />
        <text x={X0 + i * CELL + CELL / 2} y="82" text-anchor="middle" class="b num">{v}</text>
        <text x={X0 + i * CELL + CELL / 2} y="118" text-anchor="middle" class="m num">
          <tspan data-lang-en>slot {i}</tspan>
          <tspan data-lang-vi>ô {i}</tspan>
        </text>
      </>
    ))}
    <text x="20" y="80" class="body">
      <tspan data-lang-en>Backing array, 4 slots</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Mảng nền, 4 ô</tspan>
    </text>

    <text x="20" y="168" class="body">a: len 3, cap 4</text>
    <rect x={X0} y="150" width={3 * CELL} height="26" class="goldbox" />
    <text x="20" y="208" class="body">b = append(a, 1): len 4, cap 4</text>
    <rect x={X0} y="190" width={4 * CELL} height="26" class="goldbox" />
    <text x="20" y="248" class="body">c = append(a, 2): len 4, cap 4</text>
    <rect x={X0} y="230" width={4 * CELL} height="26" class="goldbox" />

    <text x={X0 + 4 * CELL + 14} y="208" class="m">
      <tspan data-lang-en>1 goes into slot 3</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>1 vào ô 3</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x={X0 + 4 * CELL + 14} y="248" class="r">
      <tspan data-lang-en>2 overwrites it</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>2 ghi đè lên</tspan>
    </text>
    <text x="20" y="286" class="m">
      <tspan data-lang-en>The array had room, so append reused it and neither b nor c got a copy of its own.</tspan>
      <tspan data-lang-vi>Mảng còn chỗ nên append dùng lại nó, b và c không có bản sao riêng.</tspan>
    </text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Slices are small headers over an array. When cap allows, append writes into the shared array instead of copying.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Slice là header nhỏ trỏ vào một mảng. Khi cap còn đủ, append ghi thẳng vào mảng chung thay vì sao chép.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .gp20a { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .gp20a-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .gp20a svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; }
  .gp20a text { font-size: 14px; fill: var(--text-body); }
  .gp20a .h { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gp20a .b { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gp20a .body { font-size: 13.5px; fill: var(--text-body); }
  .gp20a .m { font-size: 13px; fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .gp20a .r { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--red); }
  .gp20a .num { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .gp20a .box { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .gp20a .goldbox { fill: var(--gold-tint-bg); stroke: var(--gold); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .gp20a .hot { fill: var(--red-tint-bg); stroke: var(--red); stroke-width: 1.3; }
  .gp20a figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
